66 1080 "560" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560066 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560066 1083 #uuid "3324145e-7687-5d49-96a6-669054ec659f" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560067 1080 "\\frac{416}{3}" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560067 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560067 1083 #uuid "3d11677f-b41e-53c2-82d6-2e3f223790cb" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560068 1080 "75" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560068 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560068 1083 #uuid "43db1007-ab9e-5837-ae42-58fe3ae09f69" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560069 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560081 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560069 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560069 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=5$, $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=3$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(5x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560069 1072 #uuid "44f48d44-16c7-5f68-afd1-234e4ffcf06f" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560069 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5 x + 1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =5+0+0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}5\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}5\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}5\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[5x]_{x=0}^{x=5}\\cdot (4-0)\\cdot (3-0) \\\\  & =(25-0)\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =300.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560070 1080 "18" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560070 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560070 1083 #uuid "45e66bb7-f2af-5ce9-91d0-f2364b6fe2d7" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560097 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560071 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=2$, $x=3$, $y=1$, $y=2$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560071 1072 #uuid "46a20a9b-cc15-5359-b9ee-c5e59873229e" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560071 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=2}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(27-8)\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =114.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560072 1080 "-1680" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560072 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560072 1083 #uuid "47e66ac9-ee46-5c7a-8e67-1eb9e32c798a" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560060 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560064 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560070 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560111 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560115 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1077 "selection" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560115 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560073 1079 #uuid "4c27ed1e-c805-56df-b90b-eaa5a3199381" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560074 1080 "30" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560074 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560074 1083 #uuid "4c942fa1-574a-5714-9d2d-2c69b9d82fdc" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560075 1080 "160" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560075 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560075 1083 #uuid "4f85cd44-af17-57ec-b3e1-4a6bfc979738" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560076 1080 "38" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560076 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560076 1083 #uuid "5712fa33-2654-560a-953b-8ab341a87dac" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560077 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560089 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560077 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560077 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=2$, $x=4$, $y=1$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560077 1072 #uuid "57bd4c96-69f4-548a-a5d1-44f3f174d1f7" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560077 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=4}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=4}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(64-8)\\cdot (16-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1680.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560078 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560058 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560078 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560078 1071 "L