t dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(7 x + 1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =7+0+0 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}7\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}7\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}7\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[7x]_{x=0}^{x=4}\\cdot (3-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(28-0)\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =168.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560122 1080 "190" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560122 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560122 1083 #uuid "f659541f-1b8a-5155-9cf3-659c2f25168c" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560123 1080 "42" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560123 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560123 1083 #uuid "f9b4e512-f49c-5fe5-918b-c26f5ec9835f" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560091 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560124 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560124 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=2$, $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=5$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(8x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560124 1072 #uuid "fb1a5424-5e52-51f6-a33b-f2eedeb4f7d7" 13194139536036 17592186045443 true] [17592186560124 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its c